        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Coll, Loch Breachacha, Scotland\n- Structures: Breachacha Castle, Breacachadh Castle, Dùn Dubh, hillfort\n- Topics: sandy beaches, sand dunes, corncrakes\n\nFacts:\n- Coll is known for its sandy beaches that rise into large sand dunes.\n- Coll is known for its corncrakes.\n- Coll is known for Breacachadh Castle.\n- Breachacha Castle, also spelled Breacachadh, refers to either of two structures on the shore of Loch Breachacha on the Inner Hebridean island of Coll in Scotland.\n- Dùn Dubh is a hillfort on the Inner Hebridean island of Coll.",
